  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as the speaker of the text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the child in the image, who is visually depicted as the one asking the question 'are my sins forgiven now father?'. The text explicitly uses 'my' and 'father', which deictically anchors the question to the speaker. The child, as the only visible entity, is mapped as 'me' in the text, creating a direct semiotic projection where the viewer identifies with the child's perspective and innocence. This projection is central to the meme's humor, as it juxtaposes the child's physical state (drooling, missing tooth) with the solemn religious question.",
